 triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 8 & 10 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(6,3)$, $(8,4)$ and $(10,5).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/assets/a91af151d3dc0e48aef0eef58012f6c9f72aaff02aafae2d55fe0714c29c96e3.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/state.json" "file_sha256" "53c5c0e972e801f66ce79035431092eeadb57bbe23434bd1e133d6aa4caefee5"} {"question" "q-21063" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3117cac283fb94cc19d5fe97a6acc1c3e0354b103cbb0237db3b15f187694112"} {"question" "q-21063" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/state.json" "file_sha256" "53c5c0e972e801f66ce79035431092eeadb57bbe23434bd1e133d6aa4caefee5"} {"question" "q-21063" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/assets/40f352980b38be63b071b160953eff23a98996dce58c5f616e10958a8a70182e.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question